cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Gapless MTC-locked loops (869ejxng3 + 1amfwm7e6cw, PR #22): a looping
    layer wraps on the engine's loop period (/loop/period num den frames,
    one period per file shared with the audio player) instead of being
    re-anchored by the engine every pass; a capabilities file tells
    cuems-engine >= 0.1.0rc6-7 that this VC understands it.
  * Loop tail (D15): a video shorter than the period holds its last frame
    for a tail of up to 0.5 s and draws nothing beyond (the blank-layer
    flag, cleared at the next pass; a finite loop whose tail was dark ends
    dark); a period shorter than the video cuts at the loop point (INFO
    within 0.5 s, ERROR beyond).
  * Undecodable timecode (D13): with doubled quarter frames the layer holds
    its frame after 800 ms without an anchored tick and follows again when
    the timecode decodes, the audio player's rule; ERROR names the likely
    cause (a doubled rtpmidid subscription).
  * MTC day alignment (1amfwm7fbqy, PR #18): an engine layer offset is
    converted into this process's MTC day (mtcreceiver eb7ad4f, toLocalDay,
    12 h rule), so a videocomposer restarted after the engine passed 24 h
    no longer places cues a day off; while the head is not authoritative
    the offset stays pending and is polled, never applied blind. Journal:
    "MTC day-align: ..." lines.
  * Per-output color correction (programme phase 3, PR #17): each output
    can carry brightness, contrast, saturation, hue and gamma, plus an
    optional 3D LUT (.cube, up to 65^3), applied in the output blit after
    edge blending. Set in /etc/cuems/display.conf per [output:...] with
    color_brightness= color_contrast= color_saturation= color_hue=
    color_gamma= color_lut= (a relative LUT path is resolved under
    /etc/cuems/luts/, ".." refused), or live over OSC with
    /videocomposer/display/color <connector> <param> <value> | reset |
    lut <file|none>. An output without color draws exactly as 0.1.2-11 and
    costs nothing; color on an output costs GPU (trims + 65^3 LUT on
    2x4K30 Panera: about +13 points of render busy).
  * Show lock: display color and every restart-class display command are
    refused while /tmp/cuems.show.lock exists (a project loaded) and
    applied hot otherwise, with the cause in the REFUSED line. The lock is
    written by cuems-engine >= 0.1.0rc6-6; with an older engine on any box
    nothing is gated, so install this VC only where the engine is >= rc6-6.
  * Layer and master color use the same CPU-composed color matrix as the
    outputs (brightness, contrast, saturation and hue as one 3x3 matrix +
    offset, gamma per pixel): same picture within 1/255, less GPU work.
  * output/list prints one output_color line per output after the region
    lines (which are unchanged, so the power-bridge NDI preview parser
    keeps working).
  * Master color now works on the DRM canvas (1amfwm7fp88, PR #20): master
    commands reached a dummy renderer, and the master pass rebound
    framebuffer 0 instead of the canvas, so master trims did nothing on
    every DRM show box since the feature (c592ca2). Master color is also
    right way up now. Master transforms (position, scale, rotation,
    corners) stay a no-op on DRM, now with one WARNING instead of a
    risk of a blank output.
  * Build: compiles against FFmpeg 8 (AV_CODEC_ID_AYUV guard, explicit
    <algorithm>) for CI on Ubuntu 26.04 (PR #21).
  * Verified (cuems-RELATIONS Plans/2026-10-22-vc-output-colour-phase3.md
    section 10): pixel readbacks of output, layer and master trims within
    1/255 of the CPU reference on N97 (i915) and FP530 (radeonsi), every
    shader compiles on both; frame cadence with color equal to the cadence
    without it at 25/29.97/30@60, 29.97/25@50 and 3x60 fps layers; by eye
    on .111 and the test controller (2026-10-28 .. 11-02).
  * Test aids, both OFF unless their variable is set (PR #12, PR #14):
    - CadenceStats: VIDEOCOMPOSER_CADENCE_STATS=1 logs one line per output
      and layer every 60 s with the presented-frame cadence in vsyncs
      (holds histogram, outside-pattern holds, skips, steps back, wraps,
      discontinuities); coupled pacing path only.
    - OutputSnapshot: VIDEOCOMPOSER_SNAPSHOT_DIR=<dir> makes kill -USR2
      write one post-blit PPM per output into <dir>. Each round stalls
      the render loop (~50-90 ms at 2x4K, one MTC snap): never on a show.
    Used by the phase-3 and 869ejxng3 rig rounds to check the shipped deb
    (identity picture per output, cadence at loop wraps).
  * Install together with the rest of the 869ejxng3 batch: cuems-engine
    0.1.0rc6-7, cuems-audioplayer 0.0.3-15, cuems-utils 0.1.0rc18,
    cuems-editor 0.1.0rc1-8; the whole cluster takes it at once.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 01:30:26 +0100

cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-11) unstable; urgency=high

  * Sync: content at the MTC rate (25 fps) now goes through the smooth clock
    and the cadence smoother like every other rate. It used to take the raw
    MTC frame from the quarter-frame-quantised head, so under load 25 fps on
    a 60 Hz output showed about one single-vsync frame per second (jumps
    inside the 3:2 cadence). Measured on .111: from ~1.0/s to 0 in 140 s,
    a clean 3:2; confirmed by eye on 25@60, 29.97@50 and 29.97@60.
  * Regression test Integration_FramerateConverter_SameRateFollowsTimeNotRawFrame
    (fails without the fix, passes with it; suite 101/101 on an N97).

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 20 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0200

cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-10) unstable; urgency=high

  * Frame pacing: coupled pacing (every output presents on the slowest
    CRTC's vblank, one atomic commit for all) is the default again.
    Per-surface pacing (PR #8, 869emcrwa) shipped as default in 0.1.2-9 and
    regressed multi-output playback: the loop woke once per CRTC flip, the
    MTC rate estimator sampled 10 ms head steps across 1-5 ms sibling wakes
    and the smooth clock was hard-snapped back 11 ms several times a second
    (`MIDISync: anti-drift SNAP errorMs=-11`), and the cadence smoother
    counted those wakes as vsyncs and lost its minimum hold. Per-surface
    pacing stays opt-in: VIDEOCOMPOSER_PER_SURFACE_PACING=1 (mixed-refresh
    canvases only, not yet validated for stutter-free playback).
    VIDEOCOMPOSER_COUPLED_PACING=1 still forces coupled.
  * MIDISyncSource: the MTC rate is sampled over >= 500 ms windows and
    clamped to +-5 % (independent of the poll cadence); also removes the rare
    +11..+19 ms snaps 0.1.2-6 logged at 2x4K30.
  * Regression test Integration_MIDISyncSource_RateWindowImmuneToPollCadence
    (fails on the 0.1.2-9 estimator, passes here; suite 100/100 on an N97).
  * Verified by eye on .111 (2026-10-20): stock 0.1.2-9 with two outputs
    shows the jumps; this build plays a 60 fps clip over three decoding
    layers on a single matched output without a hitch.
  * Analysis: cuems-RELATIONS Plans/2026-10-20-vc-per-surface-pacing-
    stutter-review.md. FP530 operators: a mixed-refresh canvas is back on
    the pre-PR #8 behaviour (paced by the slowest CRTC) unless opted in.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 20 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0200

cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * FP530 campaign (ClickUp 869en65tm; PR #8, supersedes #2):
    - Per-CRTC frame pacing: each refresh-rate class flips on its own vblank,
      so mixed refresh rates no longer break the canvas (869emcrwa).
    - Decode path: the synchronous decoder is gone (probe context only,
      freed at once) - one hardware decode context per layer instead of two.
      An 8 GB FP530 now survives a 4-layer fade show for 5 h; 0.1.2-7
      starved it in 14 min.
    - G12 hang guard, saturation monitor and machine profiles (keyed on the
      GPU). The cue refusal is OFF by default: --hang-guard=on enforces the
      measured cap, --hang-guard=off disarms everything; counts, advisories
      and saturation warnings always run.
    - The compositor's death is reported (exit reporter); recovery-policy
      tests.

